# Environment Variables

## Backend (.env)
copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values:

```env
# Project
PROJECT_NAME=Business Listing Platform
VERSION=1.0.0

# Database
POSTGRES_USER=blp_user
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme
POSTGRES_DB=blp_db
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# Redis
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# Security
SECRET_KEY=change-this-in-production
ALGORITHM=HS256
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=30

# External APIs
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
BING_MAPS_API_KEY=
OPENSTREETMAP_NOMINATIM_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org

# Frontend
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/oauth/google/callback
META_OAUTH_APP_ID=
META_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/oauth/meta/callback

# File uploads
UPLOAD_DIR=uploads
MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE=10485760
```

## Frontend (Vite)
Vite exposes environment variables prefixed with `VITE_` on `import.meta.env`.
No special env file is required for development; use `.env.local` for local overrides.
